   "stem": {
      "text": "Let F be the antiderivative of \\( f(x) = \\frac{x + 1}{x^{2} + 2 x + 2} \\) with \\( F(1) = 2 \\). Find the exact value of \\( F\\left(3\\right) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Ln",
               [
                  "Rational",
                  17,
                  5
               ]
            ],
            2
         ],
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x^{2} + 2 x + 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               "x"
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then \\( du = \\left(2 x + 2\\right) \\, dx \\), so \\( \\left(x + 1\\right) \\, dx = \\frac{1}{2} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Since \\( F(3) = F(1) + \\int_{1}^{3} \\frac{x + 1}{x^{2} + 2 x + 2} \\, dx \\), convert the limits: \\( x = 1 \\) gives \\( u = 5 \\) and \\( x = 3 \\) gives \\( u = 17 \\), so the integral becomes \\( \\int_{5}^{17} \\frac{1}{2 u} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            1,
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               "u"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "An antiderivative of \\( \\frac{1}{2 u} \\) is \\( \\frac{\\ln{\\left(u \\right)}}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Ln",
               "u"
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "The integral is \\( \\frac{\\ln{\\left(17 \\right)}}{2} - \\left(\\frac{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}{2}\\right) = \\frac{\\ln{\\left(\\frac{17}{5} \\right)}}{2} \\), so \\( F(3) = 2 + \\frac{\\ln{\\left(\\frac{17}{5} \\right)}}{2} = \\frac{\\ln{\\left(\\frac{17}{5} \\right)}}{2} + 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
